== bench/gemm_price_main.mojo [IDENTICAL] ==
profile mojolearn.identical.gemm.fp32.v1
arm device
THIS ARM IS A GPU LEG (contract 13.5, assumption A5), in BOTH directions: it is contaminated by any other lane's GPU work on this box AND it contaminates theirs. tools/gemm_price.sh looks for a concurrent mojo/pixi process at both ends and reports what it found; it does not refuse, so read that line.
EVERY DEVICE NUMBER BELOW IS INDICATIVE. The M4's governor pins at MINIMUM clock under heat -- 96% of an 11-second trace while 93.8% busy -- and drifts up to 1.7x across twenty minutes. Timing is the identity lane's to certify and nothing here is a certification.

check_op_encodings_are_not_interchangeable OK: table (NT,TN,NN) = (0,1,2) -> oracle (1,2,0)
check_device_op_encoding_matches_the_kernel OK: all 20 rows match contract section 3 through the KERNEL's own stride function; 20 would address DIFFERENTLY if the table code were passed raw
check_fold_sweep_k_realizes_the_p_sweep OK: all 8 swept P realized exactly through k; 2 of them CARRY (P=1018 at k=131200, L=129, carries 2 levels; P=1024 carries 0)
check_serial_fold_probe_is_the_other_topology OK: agree at P=1 and P=2, separate by 6 at F5's P=8 (tree 16777222.0 vs serial 16777216.0 )
check_workspace_formula_matches_contract_13_5 OK: all three of 13.5's stated figures (128 MiB, 2 GiB, 64 GiB) reproduced from contract_leaf_size and m*n*P*4

