   launches is fused/staged, from the launcher and not from 13.6.2's arithmetic. st/fu above 1.00 is the staged arm costing more; the workspace columns are why it can cost more for a reason that is NOT the launches, since the staged plan also stages every interior node of the tree and the fused plan stages only level 0.
   13.7: if the staged arm is slow the answer is to fuse levels into one block, which is legal and produces the same bits. It is NEVER to change the pairing.

-- 13.6.3  end to end over bench/gemm_shapes.mojo --
   FIVE ARMS. host: oracle (normative v1) and serial (diagnostic whole-k chain). device: the v1 kernel, the FAST vendor matmul, and the shipped pinned kernel -- 13.6.3's three. DEVICE TIMES ARE INDICATIVE (one thermally unstable M4; timing is the identity lane's to certify).
   m and n are CAPPED to a 2000000 MAC budget on the host arms and to a 50000000000 MAC budget on the device arms; k is EXACT on both, so L, P, the ragged tail and the tree are the full shape's. Per-cell price is measured; full-shape host cost is DERIVED by multiplication (contract 0.3: cells are independent).
